═══ impact-plan ═══
putnami impact-plan

Emit the impacted plan of the exact commit delta from --base to the checked-out HEAD for a comma-separated command list: the changed files, the impacted projects, and every task the engine plans for those commands. An extension reads this ImpactPlan instead of importing the CLI, and derives its own document from it, such as a ChangePlan. The worktree must be clean and --base must be a HEAD ancestor. Source contents, environment values, secrets, command arguments, and output paths are never emitted

Usage:
  putnami impact-plan <commands> --base <commit> [--head <commit>] [--no-cache] [--output <format>]

Command Flags:
  --base <commit>              Required base commit or ref; emitted as its full immutable commit SHA
  --head <commit>              Optional head commit or ref; it must resolve to the checked-out HEAD

Examples:
  putnami impact-plan test,build --base origin/main --output=json
  putnami impact-plan lint --base 0123456789abcdef0123456789abcdef01234567 --no-cache --output=jsonl

Global Options:
  Common: --verbose, --debug, --help
  Project Selection: --all, --impacted, --projects, --tag, --exclude-tag, --baseline
  Execution: --credential-fd, --no-cache
  Output: --output, --json, --quiet, --color, --no-color

Related Commands:
  putnami projects list
  putnami sessions inspect

