═══ cache verify ═══
putnami cache verify

Run the workspace gate tasks (the blocking commands of putnami.ci.json; lint, test and build without one) twice in isolated worktrees, compare cache keys and captured artifacts, restore the first run into a pristine tree, and fail on undeclared writes or live-versus-hit differences; declared ambient key inputs are reported without failing

Usage:
  putnami cache verify [--projects <selector> | --impacted | --all] [--exclude <names>] [--impacted-strict] [--profile <profile>] [--retry <n>] [--cpu-policy <policy>] [--trace-profile <path>] [--continue-on-error] [--output <format>]

Command Flags:
  --exclude <names>            Leave these projects out of the verified runs
  --impacted-strict            Fail when the --impacted baseline can't be resolved
  --profile <profile>          Deployment profile the verified runs use: dev | test | production
  --retry <n>                  Retry transient failures in the verified runs
  --cpu-policy <policy>        CPU ceiling policy: critical-path | measured
  --trace-profile <path>       Write the trace events of the last verified run (Chrome trace format)
  --continue-on-error          Don't abort a verified run on the first failure

Examples:
  putnami cache verify --projects /my/project
  putnami cache verify --all --output=jsonl

Global Options:
  Common: --verbose, --debug, --help
  Project Selection: --all, --impacted, --projects, --tag, --exclude-tag, --baseline
  Execution: --credential-fd, --no-cache
  Output: --output, --json, --quiet, --color, --no-color

Related Commands:
  putnami cache clean

